@startuml
title Controle de Frota — Diagrama de Arquitetura DevOps (Pipeline CI/CD)

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  BorderColor black
  FontStyle bold
}
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam folder {
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  BorderColor black
}
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FEFFDD
  BorderColor black
}

actor "Desenvolvedor" as dev

node "GitHub" as github {
  component "Repositório\npraticas-extensionistas-iv\n(branch main)" as repo
  component "GitHub Actions\n(workflow CI/CD)" as actions
  database "GitHub Container\nRegistry (GHCR)" as ghcr
}

node "Servidor de Produção (VPS)" as prodserver {
  component "Docker Compose\n(serviços: web + db)" as compose
  component "Aplicação em execução\n(Apache/PHP-FPM + MySQL)" as running
}

dev --> repo : git push (main) /\npull request

repo --> actions : dispara o workflow\n(on: push, pull_request)

actions --> actions : Job 1 — Build & Test\n(composer install,\nphpunit, phpcs/phpstan)

actions --> ghcr : Job 2 — Build & Push\n(docker build -t app:sha\ndocker push)

actions --> prodserver : Job 3 — Deploy\n(SSH action:\ndocker compose pull && up -d)

ghcr --> compose : pull da imagem\nmais recente

compose --> running : sobe/atualiza os\ncontainers (rolling update)

note bottom of actions
  Pipeline (.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml):
  1) lint + testes automatizados
  2) build da imagem Docker da aplicação
  3) push para o GHCR (registry privado)
  4) deploy remoto via SSH na VPS,
     reiniciando os containers com a
     nova imagem (docker compose up -d)
end note

note right of prodserver
  Observabilidade: docker logs / healthcheck
  do Compose; alertas simples via
  GitHub Actions (job de deploy falha
  = notificação por e-mail ao time).
end note

@enduml
